# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pengenalan {#introduction}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the Qiskit in the Classroom modules, you'll have the opportunity to use a quantum computer to explore various concepts in quantum computing-adjacent fields such as quantum mechanics, computer science, chemistry, and more. This module serves as a prerequisite to the others - it introduces the fundamentals of quantum computing and how to use Qiskit to run quantum circuits.\n"
msgstr "Dalam modul Qiskit dalam Bilik Darjah, Anda akan berpeluang menggunakan komputer kuantum untuk meneroka pelbagai konsep dalam bidang berkaitan pengkomputeran kuantum seperti mekanik kuantum, sains komputer, kimia, dan lain-lain. Modul ini berfungsi sebagai prasyarat kepada modul-modul yang lain — ia memperkenalkan asas pengkomputeran kuantum dan cara menggunakan Qiskit untuk menjalankan litar kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First we'll give you a brief overview of how a classical computer works, then we'll show you how these concepts are adapted to fit the quantum computing paradigm. Finally, we'll show you how to put these concepts together to build and execute your first quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pertama kita akan memberi gambaran ringkas tentang cara komputer klasik berfungsi, kemudian kita akan tunjukkan bagaimana konsep-konsep ini disesuaikan untuk memenuhi paradigma pengkomputeran kuantum. Akhirnya, kita akan tunjukkan cara menggabungkan konsep-konsep ini untuk membina dan melaksanakan litar kuantum pertama Anda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical computers {#classical-computers}"
msgstr "Komputer klasik {#classical-computers}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You're likely familiar with the basics of how classical computers work, but here we'll highlight a few of the key features so that we can then draw a comparison to quantum computers.\n"
msgstr "Kamu mungkin sudah biasa dengan asas cara komputer klasik berfungsi, tetapi di sini kita akan menyerlahkan beberapa ciri utama supaya kita boleh membuat perbandingan dengan komputer kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basic units of information: bits {#the-basic-units-of-information-bits}"
msgstr "Unit maklumat asas: bit {#the-basic-units-of-information-bits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical computers process classical information, and the fundamental unit of classical information is the *bit*. A single bit can store the answer to one \"yes/no\" question. We usually represent the two binary states of a bit as \"0\" and \"1\".\n"
msgstr "Komputer klasik memproses maklumat klasik, dan unit asas maklumat klasik ialah *bit*. Satu bit boleh menyimpan jawapan kepada satu soalan \"ya/tidak\". Kita biasanya mewakili dua keadaan binari sebuah bit sebagai \"0\" dan \"1\".\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Review of binary numbers {#review-of-binary-numbers}"
msgstr "Ulasan nombor binari {#review-of-binary-numbers}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining bits enables you to store more information. For example, if you want to store a number from 0 to 15, you could do so with four bits in the following way:\n"
msgstr "Menggabungkan bit membolehkan Anda menyimpan lebih banyak maklumat. Contohnya, jika Anda ingin menyimpan nombor dari 0 hingga 15, Anda boleh melakukannya dengan empat bit seperti berikut:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|  | |  | |\n"
"| :------- | :------: | :-------: | -------: |\n"
"| 0 = 0000     |4 = 0100  | 8 = 1000    | 12 = 1100 |\n"
"| 1 = 0001  | 5 = 0101  | 9 = 1001  | 13 = 1101 |\n"
"| 2 = 0010  | 6 = 0110  | 10 = 1010   | 14 = 1110 |\n"
"| 3 = 0011  | 7 = 0111   | 11 = 1011  | 15 = 1111|\n"
msgstr ""
"|  | |  | |\n"
"| :------- | :------: | :-------: | -------: |\n"
"| 0 = 0000     |4 = 0100  | 8 = 1000    | 12 = 1100 |\n"
"| 1 = 0001  | 5 = 0101  | 9 = 1001  | 13 = 1101 |\n"
"| 2 = 0010  | 6 = 0110  | 10 = 1010   | 14 = 1110 |\n"
"| 3 = 0011  | 7 = 0111   | 11 = 1011  | 15 = 1111|\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, to convert from a binary number of $N$ bits to a familiar, base-10 number, you multiply the least-significant (rightmost) bit by $2^0 = 1$, the next bit to the left by $2^1 = 2$, then the next by $2^2 = 4$, and so on, until you reach the most significant (leftmost bit), which you multiply $2^{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr "Secara umum, untuk menukar nombor binari $N$ bit kepada nombor asas-10 yang biasa, Anda darabkan bit paling kurang bererti (paling kanan) dengan $2^0 = 1$, bit seterusnya ke kiri dengan $2^1 = 2$, kemudian seterusnya dengan $2^2 = 4$, dan seterusnya, sehingga Anda mencapai bit paling bererti (bit paling kiri), yang Anda darabkan dengan $2^{N-1}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So, that means that $N$ bits can be in one of $2^N$ different possible states.\n"
msgstr "Jadi, itu bermakna $N$ bit boleh berada dalam salah satu daripada $2^N$ keadaan yang berbeza.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman Anda {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Jawapan">
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "How many bits would you need to represent the number 86? Write out the bitstring that encodes this number in binary.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Ingat, $N$ bit
# membolehkan Anda mewakili nombor $0$ hingga $
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember, $N$ bits allows you to represent the numbers $0$ through $2^N - 1$, so using six bits would get us up to $2^6 - 1 = 63$. That's not quite enough. We add one more bit to get up to $2^7 - 1 = 127$. Now let's break 86 down into powers of 2:\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"86 &= 64 + 16 + 4 + 2 \\\\\n"
"&= 2^6 \\times 1 + 2^5 \\times 0 + 2^4 \\times 1 + 2^3 \\times 0 + 2^2 \\times 1 + 2^1 \\times 1 + 2^0 \\times 0 \\\\\n"
"&= 1010110\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
