# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single bit in a classical computer can only hold the value 0 or 1.\n"
msgstr "Satu bit dalam komputer klasik hanya boleh menyimpan nilai 0 atau 1.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entanglement means the state of one qubit is independent of the state of another.\n"
msgstr "Keterjalin bermakna keadaan satu qubit adalah bebas daripada keadaan qubit yang lain.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum gates are generally irreversible operations.\n"
msgstr "get kuantum umumnya adalah operasi yang tidak boleh dibalikkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit convention places the least significant qubit, $q_0$, at the leftmost position.\n"
msgstr "Konvensyen Qiskit meletakkan qubit paling tidak signifikan, $q_0$, di kedudukan paling kiri.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring a quantum state always gives the exact same result if repeated many times.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur keadaan kuantum sentiasa memberikan keputusan yang sama jika diulang berkali-kali.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate creates superposition in a single qubit.\n"
msgstr "get Hadamard mencipta superposisi dalam satu qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuits may include measurement operations that collapse the superposition state into one of the classically allowed states.\n"
msgstr "litar kuantum mungkin merangkumi operasi pengukuran yang meruntuhkan keadaan superposisi kepada salah satu keadaan yang dibenarkan secara klasik.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of possible classical states for $N$ bits is $2N$.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan keadaan klasik yang mungkin untuk $N$ bit ialah $2N$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The outcome probabilities for quantum measurements are given by the squared amplitudes of the classically measurable basis states.\n"
msgstr "Kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran kuantum diberikan oleh amplitud kuasa dua keadaan asas yang boleh diukur secara klasik.\n"

